# @epistemologic/property/docblock_no_extraction_pattern — third
# of the trio of #53 property/fracture bilateral instances at
# doc-claim altitude. Sixth #53 family overall (third-of-trio
# slot); landed per Seam Phase D ratification chain:
#   - `820a451` TICK 1 `shards/docblock.mirror` family-root RATIFY
#   - `3283de4` TICK 2 `shards/epistemologic/liquid_extraction.mirror`
#     sibling family-root RATIFY
#   - `ff53d46` TICK 3 `docblock_grounded` (first-of-trio declarative
#     half) RATIFY-WITH-CORRECTIONS
#   - `9b0aeb5` TICK 4 `@kintsugi/fracture/docblock_ungrounded`
#     (first-of-trio operational half) RATIFY
#   - `83bbdc8` TICK 5 `docblock_coherent` (second-of-trio
#     declarative half) RATIFY
#   - `caab92f` TICK 6 `@kintsugi/fracture/docblock_incoherent`
#     (second-of-trio operational half) RATIFY
# Interpretation B canonical per Seam pre-review
# `docs/audits/2026-07-06-seam-arc-4-sub-arc-a-pre-review.md` §1:
# narrative ABOVE `---`; `in` clauses + typed declarations BELOW.
#
# This shard is the DECLARATIVE HALF of the docblock extraction-
# pattern audit. The OPERATIONAL HALF lands at TICK 8 as
# `@kintsugi/fracture/docblock_extractive` per Mara spec
# `docs/specs/doc-code-seam-shards.md` §8. Bilateral discipline
# per recognition #53: the property side names WHAT it means for
# a docblock to be free of extractive patterns; the fracture side
# names WHAT TO DO when a docblock's claims exhibit an extractive
# shape (three-way routing per §8 forward-promise below).
#
# === Sixth #53 family; third-of-trio at doc-claim altitude ===
#
# Recognition #53 (`[[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]`)
# names a substrate pattern: declarative property at
# `@epistemologic/property/<predicate>` + operational fracture body
# at `@kintsugi/fracture/<predicate>`, bridged by the kintsugi loop.
# The docblock trio (`docblock_grounded`, `docblock_coherent`,
# `docblock_no_extraction_pattern`) IS the sixth #53 family
# expressed as three property/fracture bilateral pairs; each pair
# lands atomically per the #53 discipline.
#
# Trio slot ordering per Mara spec §3/§5/§7:
#
# - `docblock_grounded` (TICK 3 declarative `ff53d46`; TICK 4
#   operational `9b0aeb5`) — first-of-trio, ancestry check.
# - `docblock_coherent` (TICK 5 declarative `83bbdc8`; TICK 6
#   operational `caab92f`) — second-of-trio, non-contradiction
#   check.
# - `docblock_no_extraction_pattern` — THIS SHARD (declarative
#   half; TICK 7). Operational half at TICK 8
#   (`@kintsugi/fracture/docblock_extractive`) forward-promised
#   with three-way routing.
#
# The three bilaterals are INDEPENDENT at the declarative altitude:
# `docblock_grounded` composes over ancestor-existence;
# `docblock_coherent` composes over pairwise-non-contradiction plus
# below-seam-non-contradiction; `docblock_no_extraction_pattern`
# composes over four sub-checks (superlatives, hedges, citation-
# content-match, claim-size-match). Aggregation into
# `docblock_well_audited` happens at @docblock's family-root
# (TICK 1). Each declarative property's fracture body routes
# independently through `@kintsugi/surface` on the class the
# specific failure names — with THIS predicate's fracture body
# uniquely routing THREE-WAY per §8 (one class per sub-check
# plus a kind-reclassification path).
#
# This shard imports `@epistemologic/liquid_extraction` because
# extraction-pattern decidability lifts through the extractor's
# output shape: each of the four sub-checks reads either the
# extracted predicate text (sub-checks 1, 2) or the citation
# resolution (sub-check 3) or the below-seam declaration size
# (sub-check 4). The `in @epistemologic/liquid_extraction` grounds
# the sibling coupling to TICK 2's sibling family-root (`3283de4`);
# the extractor's `extract_predicate` output surface IS the input
# to all four sub-checks.
#
# === Predicate substance per Mara spec §7 ===
#
# The docblock-no-extraction-pattern predicate answers: is every
# extracted predicate in `d` free of the four extractive shapes
# the substrate rejects? In substrate narrative:
#
#   docblock_no_extraction_pattern(d) ⇔
#     no_unmarked_superlatives(d)
#   ∧ hedged_claims_marked_defer(d)
#   ∧ citations_content_match(d)
#   ∧ claim_size_matches_landing_size(d)
#
# ALL FOUR sub-checks must bound. Any one unbounded ⇒ predicate
# unbounded ⇒ `audit_docblock` routes to `overreach` — the
# unique verdict class the @docblock family-root reserves for
# extraction-pattern failure (per TICK 1's landed
# `docblock_verdict` type carrier's `overreach` variant). This
# is the load-bearing routing property: `overreach` is the
# substrate's name for a docblock that OVER-CLAIMS what its
# landing evidence bounds — the extractive shape #53 catches
# at this altitude.
#
# Four composed sibling predicates (one per sub-check):
#
# - `no_unmarked_superlatives(d)` reads each extracted predicate's
#   text for superlative shape ("best", "always", "never",
#   "guaranteed", "cannot fail", "perfect", "complete", etc.).
#   The sub-check fires when a superlative appears WITHOUT a
#   substrate-honoring marker (`motivating_claim` kind exemption,
#   or an adjacent forward-promise, or a citation whose ancestor
#   content matches the superlative bound). Marked superlatives
#   pass; unmarked superlatives fail. Failure routes via
#   `ashby_mismatch` (compiler-error-surface §3.1): the doc
#   channel claims more variety than the code channel can absorb
#   — Ashby's requisite variety violated at doc-claim altitude,
#   with the doc side over-claiming the axis-space the landed
#   code covers.
#
# - `hedged_claims_marked_defer(d)` reads each extracted predicate
#   for hedge shape ("might", "may", "could", "possibly",
#   "perhaps", "seems to", etc.). Hedges are LEGITIMATE at
#   substrate altitude — the substrate honors uncertainty as
#   first-class content — but hedged claims MUST carry a `defer`
#   marker naming the future tick at which the hedge closes
#   (either promotes to `grounded_claim` or retracts). Unmarked
#   hedges are the extractive shape: the doc side leaves the
#   substrate uncertain about when the substrate can decide.
#   This sub-check DOES NOT route to a surface class; it routes
#   to `@epistemologic/liquid_extraction` for
#   kind-reclassification (per Mara spec §8: deterministic
#   rewrite; no reader-frame surfacing needed because the fix
#   is mechanical — add the `defer` marker and specify the
#   closure tick).
#
# - `citations_content_match(d)` reads each extracted predicate's
#   citation and verifies the cited ancestor's content bytes
#   ground the claim's assertion. This is the sharper form of
#   `docblock_grounded`'s citation content match — but where
#   `docblock_grounded` asks whether the citation EXISTS and
#   MATCHES, this sub-check asks whether the citation is IN-BAND
#   for the claim it grounds. An out-of-band citation is one
#   where the ancestor exists and the content matches the claim
#   at surface but the ancestor's content is at a different
#   altitude, or different scope, or different frame than the
#   claim's grounding requires. Failure routes via `out_of_band`
#   (compiler-error-surface §3.4): the citation opens a channel
#   the substrate cannot bind at the frame the claim needs.
#
# - `claim_size_matches_landing_size(d)` compares the extracted
#   predicate's claim scope against the below-seam landing scope
#   on the shard. A claim that names "the substrate's foundational
#   discipline" grounded by a single below-seam type declaration
#   is a size mismatch: the claim's variety-axis-space exceeds
#   the landing's variety-axis-space. Failure routes via
#   `contradiction` (compiler-error-surface §3.2): the doc-side
#   claim and the code-side landing contradict at scope-arithmetic
#   altitude — the two channels cannot simultaneously hold on the
#   same shard because the claim's implicit universal quantifier
#   fires success while the landing's below-seam declarations
#   witness only a proper subset of what the claim covers.
#
# === Three-way routing per Mara spec §8 (forward-promise) ===
#
# The operational half `@kintsugi/fracture/docblock_extractive`
# at TICK 8 routes DIFFERENTLY per sub-check — the substrate's
# first three-way routing fracture body:
#
# - Sub-check 1 (`no_unmarked_superlatives` unbounded) →
#   `ashby_mismatch` per compiler-error-surface §3.1.
# - Sub-check 3 (`citations_content_match` unbounded) →
#   `out_of_band` per compiler-error-surface §3.4.
# - Sub-check 4 (`claim_size_matches_landing_size` unbounded) →
#   `contradiction` per compiler-error-surface §3.2.
# - Sub-check 2 (`hedged_claims_marked_defer` unbounded) →
#   `@epistemologic/liquid_extraction` kind-reclassification
#   (deterministic rewrite; no reader-frame surfacing).
#
# This three-way plus one is structural: `overreach` is the
# @docblock family-root's single routing verdict, but the fracture
# body operationalizes it as FOUR distinct kintsugi loops — three
# through `@kintsugi/surface` and one through the liquid-extraction
# rewrite path. The trio's first two bilaterals routed one-way
# (docblock_ungrounded → ashby_mismatch; docblock_incoherent →
# contradiction); this bilateral is the first to route three-way
# on the surface side and to add a fourth deterministic-rewrite
# path. Bilateral pattern #53 absorbs this variance without new
# structural primitives — the fracture body is still a single
# @kintsugi/fracture/* action; the routing surface at
# @kintsugi/surface still names each class; the substrate's
# ashby_variety_match still discharges each dispatch.
#
# === Sibling coupling to @docblock + @epistemologic/liquid_extraction ===
#
# This shard's `in @docblock` grounds the sibling-coupling to
# TICK 1's family-root (`5c0f5ba` + `820a451` RATIFY): the
# `docblock` carrier the property predicate takes as input is
# exactly @docblock's typed carrier, and the `overreach` verdict
# variant is the routing target this predicate's unbounded case
# reserves. The `in @epistemologic/liquid_extraction` grounds
# the sibling-coupling to TICK 2's family-root (`32a1e2a` +
# `3283de4` RATIFY): the extractor's output shape
# (`predicate_shape` splinter(ast) fragment) is the surface all
# four sub-checks discharge over. Both sibling family-roots are
# COUPLED via this shard: extraction-pattern audit is a question
# the substrate can only ask at the intersection of the doc-claim
# carrier and the liquid-extraction surface.
#
# This shard also imports `in @epistemologic/property` (species-
# family path) per the six sibling properties already landed at
# that altitude: `cold_compile_within_tolerance`,
# `dark_count_monotone`, `restart_intensity_well_formed`,
# `docblock_grounded`, and `docblock_coherent`. The path-namespace
# pact carries the depth-2 discipline for all species members.
#
# === Path-namespace property ===
#
# This file at
# `shards/epistemologic/property/docblock_no_extraction_pattern.mirror`
# declares `@epistemologic/property/docblock_no_extraction_pattern`
# at species-depth 2 under @epistemologic per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`. The depth mirrors
# the six landed siblings at `@epistemologic/property/{
# cold_compile_within_tolerance, dark_count_monotone,
# restart_intensity_well_formed, docblock_grounded,
# docblock_coherent}`: this shard sits in the same species column
# and is subject to the same path-namespace pact.
#
# === Circular-reflexive self-audit ===
#
# Per Mara's projection-surface spec `63bdecc` §6 the operator
# must audit its own audit at depth=3. This shard's own docblock
# is subject to `docblock_no_extraction_pattern(this_docblock)`
# at logical altitude. Substrate-honest verdict at THIS shard's
# state on all four sub-checks:
#
# - Sub-check 1 (`no_unmarked_superlatives`): the narrative above
#   uses "load-bearing" and "canonical" but each appears in a
#   substrate-honoring frame (`load-bearing predicate` names the
#   substrate's own load-bearing discipline; `Interpretation B
#   canonical` cites the Seam pre-review document that ratifies
#   the discipline). "First three-way routing fracture body"
#   names a factual first — not a superlative on quality but a
#   count on the substrate's routing surface. No unmarked
#   superlative fires at analytical altitude.
#
# - Sub-check 2 (`hedged_claims_marked_defer`): the narrative
#   above hedges on TICK 8's exact routing shape ("first
#   three-way routing fracture body"). The hedge is anchored to
#   a `forward_promise` naming TICK 8 as the closure tick; the
#   substrate's `defer` marker is the forward-promise itself
#   per @docblock's carrier surface. No unmarked hedge fires.
#
# - Sub-check 3 (`citations_content_match`): the narrative above
#   cites seven ratification commits (`820a451`, `3283de4`,
#   `ff53d46`, `9b0aeb5`, `83bbdc8`, `caab92f`, and the two
#   sibling family-root landings `5c0f5ba`, `32a1e2a`), plus
#   substrate document paths (Mara spec §7, §8; compiler-error-
#   surface §3.1, §3.2, §3.4; projection-surface §6; Seam
#   pre-review §1). Each citation resolves to an ancestor on
#   main; each ancestor's content grounds the claim it appears
#   in at the frame the claim needs (spec sections cited by
#   number map to the spec's actual sections; commit OIDs cited
#   are the Seam ratification chain preceding this landing).
#   Concrete byte-match awaits the extractor body (TICK 2
#   forward-promise).
#
# - Sub-check 4 (`claim_size_matches_landing_size`): the
#   narrative above makes claims at three scopes: (i) claims
#   about THIS shard's below-seam declarations (the prism block
#   and predicate signature); (ii) claims about the trio's
#   internal ordering (grounded by the six preceding ratification
#   commits); (iii) claims about the sixth #53 family membership
#   (grounded by the five preceding #53 family instances).
#   Each claim's scope matches its landing size: (i) matches the
#   below-seam prism + predicate; (ii) matches the six Seam
#   ratification commits; (iii) matches the five prior family
#   citations. No claim exceeds its landing.
#
# Verdict: `both_survive` — the shard's docblock passes real
# survival on all four sub-checks at analytical altitude but
# phantom survival is also non-empty (the extractor body has not
# landed; concrete byte-match on citations cannot fire until it
# does; sub-check 3's in-band check cannot concretely discriminate
# out-of-band citations at the current altitude). Promotion to
# `real_survives` awaits: extractor body (TICK 2 forward-promise)
# + fracture body at TICK 8 with three-way routing + Seam
# second-witness audit at analytical altitude on all four
# sub-checks. Per Mara spec §Cross-cutting: this is the honest
# verdict at THIS shard's state. If this docblock returned
# `real_survives` from its own self-audit here, that WOULD BE
# the phantom failure mode the discipline exists to catch.

---

in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/property
in @epistemologic/liquid_extraction
in @docblock

prism @epistemologic/property/docblock_no_extraction_pattern {
  focus docblock_no_extraction_pattern
  project docblock_no_extraction_pattern
  split docblock_no_extraction_pattern
  shift docblock_no_extraction_pattern
  settle docblock_no_extraction_pattern
}

# === docblock_no_extraction_pattern predicate (declarative half) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING PREDICATE. Returns verdict that every extracted
# predicate in `d` is free of all four extractive shapes the
# substrate rejects. Per Mara spec §7 predicate substance:
#
#   docblock_no_extraction_pattern(d) ⇔
#     no_unmarked_superlatives(d)
#   ∧ hedged_claims_marked_defer(d)
#   ∧ citations_content_match(d)
#   ∧ claim_size_matches_landing_size(d)
#
# All four sub-checks must bound. Any one unbounded ⇒ predicate
# unbounded ⇒ `audit_docblock` routes to `overreach` (the
# @docblock family-root's reserved routing verdict for
# extraction-pattern failure).
#
# Body discharges at splinter(ast) altitude via the liquid-
# extraction surface's `extract_predicate` output; the operational
# half at `@kintsugi/fracture/docblock_extractive` (TICK 8
# forward-promise per Mara spec §8) routes THREE-WAY per sub-check
# (sub-check 1 → `ashby_mismatch`, sub-check 3 → `out_of_band`,
# sub-check 4 → `contradiction`; sub-check 2 → kind-reclassification
# through `@epistemologic/liquid_extraction` deterministic rewrite).
docblock_no_extraction_pattern(d: docblock) -> verdict { \ }

out @epistemologic/property/docblock_no_extraction_pattern
out docblock_no_extraction_pattern
